# Repos the decoder suite needs checked out BESIDE it on the CI venue.
#
# Declaring a sibling here is what makes its cross-repo guards actually run. An
# UNdeclared sibling is not a neutral omission: every guard written against it
# resolves with existsSync, calls this.skip(), and the gate still prints PASS,
# so the run reports green having exercised none of them. Measured 2026-08-12,
# that gap was 19 guards (a venue carrying only xchain-encoder ran 1063 passing
# / 30 pending where a full local checkout runs 1082 / 11). See
# test/unit/sibling-coverage.test.js, which reports the surface this file leaves
# uncovered; the same gap applies to a sibling that is declared but missing.
#
# ci-dispatch.sh ships each of these at its origin/master (falling back to local
# HEAD) and REFUSES the push if one is not a checkout beside this repo, so a
# declared sibling can never be silently absent. It also removes any leftover at
# the venue, so a guard can never compare against whatever revision another
# repo's run left behind.

# Roundtrip and compiled-push-size conformance, plus taproot-envelope validator parity.
xchain-encoder
# Action-manifest conformance, the canonical ORACLE_FEE_OUTPUT_ACTIVATION map,
# and the taproot golden vectors.
xchain-documentation
# Vendored coins-registry byte-identity: BTC/LTC/DOGE/index/consensus_pin.
xchain-hub
# The FIX_OUTPUT_FANOUT registration in the indexer protocol-change table.
xchain-indexer
# AuxPoW strip parity and the dispenser safe-depth twin.
xchain-utxo-tracker
